job_description:
Your Next Challenge at Techso

Are you passionate about Product Lifecycle Management (PLM) and looking to put your Teamcenter expertise to work on large-scale transformation projects?
Do you enjoy analyzing business needs, designing innovative solutions, and helping organizations optimize their engineering processes?

Techso is looking for a PLM Functional Analyst – Teamcenter to support our clients in implementing, enhancing, and optimizing Siemens Teamcenter solutions across Canada and internationally.

In this role, you'll become a strategic advisor to our clients, contributing to every phase of the project lifecycle—from business analysis and solution design to deployment and user adoption.

Who We Are

Founded in Montreal in 2014, Techso helps organizations accelerate their digital transformation through three areas of expertise:

• IT Infrastructure Management;

• Custom Application Development;

• Product Lifecycle Management (PLM).

Our team works with recognized clients across a variety of industries, including aerospace, automotive, finance, events, and watchmaking.
At Techso, we value the quality of our projects and relationships over volume. Our core values—Fun, Trust, Efficiency, and Quality—guide both the way we work with our clients and how we collaborate as colleagues.

What You'll Do

Depending on the projects assigned to you, you will:

• Analyze client business needs and translate them into functional and technical specifications;

• Configure, implement, and customize Siemens Teamcenter modules based on business requirements;

• Design solutions that optimize PLM processes, product configuration management, and engineering workflows;

• Develop and present proof of concepts (POCs) to project stakeholders;

• Participate in or lead Teamcenter deployments, testing activities, and system integrations;

• Provide expert-level functional support for complex Teamcenter environments;

• Train and support end users to ensure successful adoption of PLM solutions;

• Prepare functional and technical documentation, including user guides and architecture documentation;

• Collaborate with technical teams, solution architects, and clients throughout the project lifecycle;

• Contribute to large-scale digital transformation initiatives with leading industrial organizations.

The Profile We're Looking For

You have:

• A Bachelor's degree in Mechanical Engineering, Computer Science, or a related field;

• A minimum of five years of experience with Siemens Teamcenter or in a similar PLM consulting role;

• Strong knowledge of Teamcenter modules, including Structure Manager, Workflow Designer, BMIDE, Change Management, and Active Workspace;

• A solid understanding of PLM architectures and implementation methodologies;

• Experience with related technologies such as SQL, Java, C/C++, JavaScript, XML, ITK, SOAP, and REST services;

• Knowledge of manufacturing, aerospace, or industrial environments using Teamcenter;

• The flexibility to travel within the Montreal area and internationally when required;

• The ability to communicate professionally in both French and English, as you will collaborate with colleagues and clients located across Quebec, Canada, and internationally;

• Strong analytical, communication, and stakeholder management skills, with the ability to simplify complex technical concepts.

Nice to Have

• Experience implementing or migrating Teamcenter solutions;

• Experience integrating PLM platforms with ERP, MES, CAD, or other enterprise systems;

• Experience in digital transformation or continuous improvement initiatives;

• Experience facilitating workshops and delivering end-user training;Experience in functional architecture or organizational change management;

• International project experience.

You don't need experience with every Teamcenter module or every industry. Above all, we're looking for a passionate PLM professional who enjoys solving business challenges and helping clients maximize the value of their digital engineering solutions.
What Techso Offers

• Strategic projects with leading organizations across Canada and internationally.

• International mobility opportunities through our consultant mobility program.

• A flexible hybrid work model adapted to project and client needs.

• Bright offices in the heart of Old Montreal, featuring a rooftop terrace.

• Complimentary breakfast, snacks, and coffee available at the office.

• A vibrant social and sports club, fully sponsored by Techso.

• The opportunity to contribute beyond client projects through internal initiatives that help shape the company's future.

• A collaborative community of experts that encourages knowledge sharing, teamwork, and continuous professional growth.

• Comprehensive private group insurance tailored to your needs.

• A culture built on Fun, Trust, Efficiency, and Quality.

